      "message": "\u003e What does \"queue is one deep\" mean? I\u0027m trying to reconcile the warning with what I see here.\n\nI suspect that the intent of this function was to have a 1 element deep queue of FDs to send out, and the fds provided would get removed after a send, or replaced by the next call. Unfortunately, that isn\u0027t what the implementation actually did.\n\n\u003e It also says \"will be sent with the next write\"\n\nThis is technically correct: it will be sent with the next write. It just doesn\u0027t mention that it\u0027ll also be sent with writes after the next write. (Changing this to \"will be sent with each following write\").\n\n\u003e and \"single ancillary message\" which makes it sound like it\u0027s a one-off but then the warning implies it\u0027s a permanent/sticky setting.\n\nBy \"delivered as a single ancillary message\", I think they mean that all of the fds are delivered as a single atomic cmsghdr, instead of one cmsghdr per fd.",
